    {1..10,12}+24    M=1/11     (0.0909)
    {1..10,12}+44    M=2/23     (0.0870)
    {1..10,12}+132   M=6/67     (0.0896)
    {1..10,12}+143   M=13/145   (0.0897)
    {2..12}+13       M=2/15     (0.1333)
    {2..12}+24       M=1/7      (0.1429)
    {2..12}+26       M=1/7      (0.1429)
    {2..12}+144      M=1/7      (0.1429)
    {2..12}+156      M=1/7      (0.1429)
  NON-base tight among GW-mechanism candidates: 0
  Published GW single-acceleration criterion, uniformly at n=12:
    its obstruction interval starts at 13-r, but gcd(r,13-r)=gcd(r,13)=1
    for every r=1,...,12; hence no nontrivial AP single acceleration is tight.
  => the sampled nearest row {1..11,24} has M=2/25; the whole published
     single-acceleration mechanism is empty here (arbitrary sporadics remain open).

==========================================================================
(D) VERDICT
==========================================================================
  VERIFIED: {1..12} is the unique tight primitive 12-set in {1..16} (1/1820)
            and no GW-mechanism large-killer candidate is tight.
  PROVED lemma: rational tight point => 13|q + residue localization.
  SEPARATE theorem: global tight-from-above + no 13-multiple => full residues.
  REDUCTION: full rigidity still needs lift/deep-sheet coherence after pinning.
  HONEST: n=12 tight-instance uniqueness is conjecturally true and verified
          only in the stated finite box/families; uniform emptiness is OPEN.
          The analogous n=13 rigidity is false (Goddyn-Wong). Not closure-critical:
          THM-758 gives M>=1/14 with tight families in the PROVED <=3-far half.
